[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **The C library has no error surface.** Both entry points return `void`, the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m only scalar parameter is `unsigned int seed`, and *every* one of its 2^32 values
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m is a valid, accepted input. There is no invalid input that the C code rejects,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m so there is no error code or sentinel to match.
