[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Mechanical derivation of the axes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The C library has **no runtime options, flags, modes, or `#ifdef`s** — the grep
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m in `ERRORS.md` shows zero `if`/`switch`/`#ifdef` branches outside loop headers.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The axes it *does* branch on are therefore the entry points, the one scalar
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m parameter, the shape of the global state, and the composition count:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis A — entry point (the full public set, lowest level first).**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `nm -D` gives exactly three:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `A1` `array` — the 0x100000-byte global; read/written directly by a consumer
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `A2` `perform_expensive_operations()` — the low-level kernel pass, `f^100`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   applied element-wise to whatever is in `array` (no wrapper, no seeding)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `A3` `long_exec(seed)` — the one-shot convenience entry: `srand` + fill with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `rand()` + 2000 × `A2` + XOR fold + `printf("%d\n")`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis B — `seed` (the only parameter).** The C passes it straight to glibc
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `srand`, which special-cases `0`, so the distinct classes are: `0`, `1`, small
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m odd/even, `INT_MAX`, `2^31` (sign bit set), `UINT_MAX`, and arbitrary 32-bit.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis C — `array` content shape.** The kernel
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `x=x*3+7; x^=x>>3; x=x-(x<<1); x=x/2+x%7` distinguishes: sign of `x` (arithmetic
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `>>`, truncating `/`, sign-following `%`), overflow of `*3+7` and `<<1`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m multiples of 7, zero, `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`, and the `[0, 2^31)` sub-range that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `rand()` actually produces (`A3` can never feed a negative value into the first
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m pass, but later passes do).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis D — composition count `k`** (how many times `A2` runs before the state is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m observed): `0, 1, 2, 3, 20, 82, 100, 2000`. `k = 2000` is what `A3` does. `k ≥ 82`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`n = k·100 ≥ 8192`) is the point where the Rust crate switches from naive
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m iteration to its cycle-accelerated path, so it is a real behavioural boundary on
